@Power-up mode lookup tables.
@
@ ALL SIX "redirect" HOOKS AND ALL 29 "data" HOOKS WERE REMOVED on 2026-10-22 after
@ they caused severe rendering corruption in-game and a crash on Hammer pickup.
@
@ WHY THE REDIRECTS WERE WRONG
@ ----------------------------
@ Each redirect wrote a word that is not an instruction. Retail and patched values are
@ both small integers (< 0x01000000) that differ by a near-constant amount:
@
@     site        retail word   patched word   delta
@     0x78C58C    0x0037FCF0    0x003BCE98     +0x3D1A8
@     0x78E604    0x0037DC70    0x003BAE18     +0x3D1A8
@     0x78E7E8    0x0037DC00    0x003BADA8     +0x3D1A8
@     0x795FF0    0x00376578    0x003B3664     +0x3D0EC
@     0x7960F8    0x003762A4    0x003B3390     +0x3D0EC
@     0x7982D8    0x00374128    0x003B11E0     +0x3D0B8
@
@ A near-constant positive delta across unrelated addresses is what you see when a
@ build's internal code layout shifted and absolute pointers were recomputed, not when
@ six independent pointers are deliberately retargeted. Note this is NOT a relink in the
@ ELF sense: the retail and reference images have byte-identical program headers (same
@ 5 segments, same file offsets, same sizes). Any shifting happened INSIDE .text.
@ We do not have a confirmed explanation for these six words, and we no longer need one:
@ the labels were wrong, which is enough to disqualify them.
@
@ The labels said "redirect to the relocated body-type/height/draw-offset table". They
@ do not. What is actually at each patched target:
@
@     retail 0x37FCF0 -> an array of pointers (0x8EAD88, 0x8E3064, 0x8EAF60, ...)
@     patched 0x3BCE98 -> ARM code (0xE30D270A = movw r2, 0xD70A)
@
@ Both sides point into .text, and the patched side points at executable instructions.
@ Nothing anywhere in either image points at 0xB493A8, where the data hooks wrote their
@ float tables. So the two halves of this file contradicted each other: the tables were
@ written to a region no reader was redirected to, and the readers were pointed at code.
@
@ The two height sites (0x795FF0, 0x7960F8) feed per-actor height and draw-offset
@ lookups, which is why rendering broke globally and immediately -- before any Hammer
@ was involved -- rather than only when the Hammer appeared.
@
@ Only `mode_six_or_ten` below is a real instruction edit, so only it survives. It is
@ load-bearing: retail's 0x1FB mode mask lacks bit 9, and 0x3FB adds it, which is what
@ makes power-up mode 10 reachable at all.

mode_six_or_ten:
    @ A gate that special-cases mode 6 now also special-cases mode 10.
    @ Retail e3500002 (cmp r0, #2) -> e350000a (cmp r0, #0xa).
    type:    instr
    instruction: cmp r0, #0xa
    address: 0x0078E6A8

@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@ REMOVED -- kept as a record, not as hooks. Do not re-enable without new evidence.
@
@   body_table_redirect_a    instr @ 0x0078C58C   target is code, not a table
@   body_table_redirect_b    instr @ 0x0078E604   target is code, not a table
@   body_table_redirect_c    instr @ 0x0078E7E8   target is code, not a table
@   height_table_redirect_a  instr @ 0x00795FF0   target is code, not a table
@   height_table_redirect_b  instr @ 0x007960F8   target is code, not a table
@   draw_offset_redirect     instr @ 0x007982D8   target is code, not a table
@
@   tall_actor_type_hammer   data  @ 0x00B0C328
@   height_table_slot_10     data  @ 0x00B493A8
@   patch_b493ac..b4942c     data  @ 0x00B493AC..0x00B4942C  (28 further words)
@
@ The data words are not lost: their values are recorded in sweetdx/docs/BUILD_FIXES.md
@ and in the original hook files under sweetdx/hooks_reference/.
@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
